---

<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1600px] px-[8%] py-32 max-lg:px-[6%] max-md:py-20 max-md:px-[6%]">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-[0.65fr_1.35fr] gap-16 max-md:grid-cols-1 max-md:gap-9">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="font-[var(--font-primary-family)] text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--accent)]">
        A little about my work
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 font-[var(--font-primary-family)] text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[var(--muted)]">
        01 — My approach
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal>
      <h2 class="max-w-[950px] font-[var(--font-heading)] text-[clamp(2.8rem,5.6vw,6rem)] font-normal leading-[1.03] tracking-[-0.045em] text-[var(--text)]">
        Good websites do more than look good.
        <span class="text-[var(--accent)]">They work beautifully, too.</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-10 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-7 max-sm:grid-cols-1 max-sm:gap-5">
        <p class="font-[var(--font-primary-family)] text-sm leading-[1.9] text-[var(--muted)]">
          Every project starts with understanding its purpose, audience and goals. The result should feel intentional, easy to use and aligned with the business behind it.
        </p>
        <p class="font-[var(--font-primary-family)] text-sm leading-[1.9] text-[var(--muted)]">
          From the first interface to the final responsive details, I focus on clean implementation, considered interactions and a consistent experience across devices.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
